  "body": "## What changed\n\n- A new catalog case `examples/catalog/3d/rest`. It follows `examples/catalog/README.md`: `model/` with its generator, `build.camscript`, `rest.camproj`, `rest.nc`, `case.toml` and `README.md`.\n- The part is original: a 60 x 50 x 4 mm plate with two 13 x 30 x 10 mm ribs. The channel between the ribs is 8 mm wide. The walls are vertical.\n- Operation 1: a 3D Pocket with a 12 mm end mill (`EM-1200-2FL`). It cannot go into the channel below the rib tops.\n- Operation 2: a 3D Pocket with a 6 mm end mill (`EM-0600-4FL`). The re-machining mask (the stock of the program ahead) limits it. It cuts only the channel. The rib ends are convex, so no rest material stands at the two mouths. The 6 mm tool enters there through space that the 12 mm tool cleared.\n- The README shows the rest region as a top view with coordinates. It names the NC lines to look at.\n- `crates/app/tests/example_catalog/case_3d_rest.rs`: the two case tests (`regenerates`, `rebuilds`) and a pin on the rest region.\n- `site/content/guide/operations/operations-3d.md`: the 3D Pocket page links the case. `cargo xtask catalog` wrote this line.\n- `docs/decisions/2867-3d-rest-case.md`: what was chosen and dropped.\n\nNo product code changed.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe catalog had no rest-machining case for 3D (#2392). An earlier note on #2867 said that no 3D operation has a rest input. The 3D Pocket reads the stock of the program ahead (M3.1 D). That is rest machining from the previous operations, so the case needs no new code.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins:\n- `catalog_3d_rest::the_small_tool_cuts_only_the_rest_region`. It reads the committed `rest.nc`. The 12 mm pocket reaches `Z4.2`. The 6 mm pocket reaches `Z4.2`. Each 6 mm feed move has its centre inside `|X| <= 2.5`, `|Y| <= 18`. Between the ribs (below `Z14`, `|Y| < 15`) the centre stays inside `|X| <= 0.8`.\n- `catalog_3d_rest::regenerates` and `catalog_3d_rest::rebuilds` (byte for byte against `rest.nc`).\n\nRed before the change: `contract::every_case_has_two_named_test_results` failed with `missing case test catalog_3d_rest::regenerates: test` when the case folder existed without its tests.\n\nMutations:\n- Re-machining mask off in `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs` (`mask_cols.as_ref().filter(|_| false)`): `build.camscript` fails at `cam.verify()` (`3D Pocket D6 rest` holds `feed moves 334 and 481 cross in XY at shared depth`). `regenerates` and `rebuilds` go red. Restored: green.\n- One 6 mm move in `rest.nc` moved to `X5.79 Y-8.387 Z12`: the region pin goes red with `6 mm feed moves outside the rest region: [(5.79, -8.387, 12.0)]`. The case was rebuilt after: green.\n\nCommands on the final head `d56e967f0`:\n- `cargo xtask catalog --check`: all cases checked, no change.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test example_catalog --test catalog_groove_part_off --test continuous_4axis_part --test example_catalog_adaptive --test example_catalog_edge_work --test first_4axis_part --test first_part_programs --test first_router_part --test tilt_basis_compat`: all green (example_catalog 47 passed, 4 ignored). These are the 9 steps of the quick plan.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Heavy reach (`cargo xtask gate heavy --base upstream/main --dry-run`): one step, `app heavy: example_catalog`. Run directly: `cargo test --release -p camcraft-app --no-fail-fast --test example_catalog -- --ignored`: 4 passed.\n\nGate note: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` failed two times in the `app build (--no-run)` step with `can't find crate for camcraft_cl` and `warning: ignoring -C extra-filename flag due to -o flag`. The sccache wrapper of the gate wrote bad artifacts into this worktree's `target/`. A plain `cargo test` then failed the same way. After `cargo clean -p` of our crates, plain cargo built and passed. So I ran the 9 planned steps and clippy directly with cargo. This is a local tool problem, not a problem of this diff.\n\nReview round 1 (head `b5919de38`): `main` (`4d891498e`) merged in. `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` with `CAMCRAFT_NO_SCCACHE=1`: 10 steps, 0 failed. `cargo xtask catalog --check`: `3d/rest` checked, no tracked file changed. `catalog_3d_rest` (3 tests): pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings`: clean. Heavy and light lanes: not run again in this round. The round changes text only and a merge of `main`.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone changed. Two new recorded programs: `examples/catalog/3d/rest/rest.nc` and `rest.camproj`. No other `*.nc`, `*.cl` or catalog file changed (`cargo xtask catalog --check` is clean).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No catalog screenshots. `cargo xtask catalog --screenshots` pushes to an images branch. The README top view and the pin show the region.\n- No light lane run: the diff has no code that a light twin covers.\n- No UI change, so no screenshots.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #4409 and #4408 add `include!` lines next to the new line in `crates/app/tests/example_catalog.rs`. Different lines; whichever merges second refreshes.\n- #4371 changes the Fanuc retract before a later tool change. `rest.nc` has a tool change (T02), so whichever merges second runs `cargo xtask catalog --case 3d/rest`.\n- #4316 changes saved catalog projects. Whichever merges second rebuilds the case the same way.\n\nChangelog: Examples: the catalog case `3d/rest` shows a 12 mm 3D Pocket, then a 6 mm 3D Pocket that cuts only the material that the 12 mm tool left (#2867)\n\nFixes #2867\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
